ounded by friends, you can feel a disconnect, as if you're merely an observer rather than a participant in the fun.\n\nAssistant:\nAssistant: Board games can indeed be hit or miss, especially depending on the game's mechanics, theme, and even the dynamics of the group playing. It's interesting how certain games can draw in participants with their intricate strategies or captivating narratives, while others can leave you feeling somewhat disinterested and detached. I wonder what types of games you generally find engaging—do you prefer competitive strategy games that challenge your intellect or perhaps cooperative games that encourage teamwork and collaboration? The variety within the realm of board games is vast, ranging from light-hearted party games that rely on humor to more complex games that require significant mental investment. It’s always a unique experience exploring different genres, and I’m curious if you have any favorites that you look forward to playing or any that have left a lasting impression on you for their fun mechanics or engaging storytelling."], "document_offset": 0, "logical_document_count": 2, "physical_batch_limit": 4, "score_contract": "pointwise", "score_space": "unit_interval", "sequence": 1044, "elapsed_seconds": 108.58643889427185}
